We add $\goldD{\dfrac{121}{16}}$ inside the parentheses, and subtract $\greenD{2}\cdot\goldD{\dfrac{121}{16}}$ outside them, to keep the expression equivalent.

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\greenD{2} \left(x^2 +\dfrac{11}{2} x\right) +15
\\\\
&=\greenD{2}\left(x^2 +\dfrac{11}{2} x+\goldD{\dfrac{121}{16}}\right) +15 -\greenD{2}\cdot\goldD{\dfrac{121}{16}}
\\\\
&=2 \left(x +\dfrac{11}{4}\right)^2 +15 -\dfrac{121}{8}
\\\\
&=2 \left(x +\dfrac{11}{4}\right)^2 -\dfrac{1}{8}
\end{align}$
